          "Defend property tax fairness and local tax burden: with 79% homeownership and $129K income, this district is acutely sensitive to property tax increases and local revenue structures; any incumbent who allows perception to develop that their party is comfortable with rising tax burdens on suburban homeowners hands the opposition a concrete grievance that overrides partisan realignment.",
          "Engage the 43% opposition specifically on their professional and family concerns: this opposition is not ideological resistance but evaluation of competence and local governance; understand whether it stems from education funding disputes, local zoning or growth management concerns, healthcare access, or other specific professional household grievances — and address those grievances directly rather than assuming they will default back to Republican identity.",
