          { name: "Generic Minority or Hispanic Community Outreach Without Specific Economic Content", tag: "avoid", why: "In a majority-Hispanic district (52.8%), token acknowledgment of Hispanic heritage or generic appeals to minority communities will not sustain constituent loyalty if the actual economic barriers facing Hispanic workers — credential access, wage stagnation for non-degreed workers, advancement pathways in specific sectors — are not being addressed with specificity. Any incumbent or challenger who treats Hispanic community engagement as a separate constituency outreach function rather than as the core of the district's economic agenda is missing the strategic reality that this is primarily a working-adult economic mobility question that happens to concentrate among the Hispanic-majority population." }
