          "Engage the Hispanic-majority community (52.8%) with specificity on their economic concerns and barriers: whether those are language access in education and employment, immigration status implications for family stability, or specific workforce development needs, avoiding generic minority outreach and instead demonstrating fluency with the particular economic constraints this community faces.",
