          "Engage healthcare policy with specificity to middle-class family economics: rising insurance premiums, prescription drug costs, and access to quality providers in competitive markets are the healthcare concerns of affluent, educated households who can afford coverage but face real cost pressures. Position legislative efforts as protecting middle-class healthcare access and cost management, not as ideological healthcare debate.",
