          "Lead on property tax fairness and rural infrastructure: the 79.6% white, homeowner-dominant, middle-income constituency is experiencing direct fiscal pressure from rising property taxes and declining rural service access. Concrete legislative accomplishments around tax relief, rural hospital sustainability, and workforce retention in the district are the baseline for holding a seat this narrow when it is actually contested.",
          "Engage the 4.56% demographic gap and Hispanic community with specificity: the 14.58% Hispanic population is not being fully captured in standard partisan analysis, but their economic concerns — affordable housing, job access, healthcare — are real and present. A representative who fails to build an active constituent relationship with the Hispanic community is leaving a swing constituency uncontested.",
