          "Address younger professional economic concerns directly: the 28.6% renter rate and demographic gap (~8%) likely represent young adults and mobile professionals for whom housing affordability, healthcare access, and quality-of-life investment matter more than partisan inheritance. Engagement on these material concerns is the pathway to holding younger voters who might otherwise default to Democratic alternatives.",
          "Investigate and specify the ~8% demographic gap: this 2,000-3,000 resident population is larger than the current margin. Understanding whether it represents multiracial households, recent immigrants, or transient young professionals—and addressing their distinct concerns—transforms the gap from a statistical artifact into a strategic opportunity.",
          "Do not treat 56% as a stable floor: in a district where the demographic profile (older, college-educated, affluent) should produce 60-65% Republican performance, the 56% result signals either swing among college-educated voters, mobilization of younger or non-white constituencies, or both. Any campaign that consolidates the existing base without addressing these vulnerabilities risks discovering in the next cycle that the margin has contracted further."
