          "Engage the 11.86% Hispanic community with specificity on professional opportunity, education access, and economic integration — not broad demographic appeals or immigration policy abstractions. This is a relatively affluent, educated Hispanic cohort in a 46.1% college-educated district; their concerns likely differ from both Democratic assumptions and Republican dismissals, and a candidate who addresses their actual economic and professional interests will find persuadable voters who have not yet committed to an opposing camp.",
